  "menuAtTheStartOfEachHandEachPlayerChooses": "At the start of each hand, each player chooses Mus to request a card exchange. If all four say Mus, everyone can discard and receive new cards. Mintza stops the Mus: you keep your hands and start bidding. Click Mintza now: only the expected button is enabled and its outline glows.",
  "menuBettingPasoAndEmbido": "Betting: Paso and Embido",
  "menuInEachPhaseYouCanBetStonesForYour": "In each phase you can bet stones for your team. Paso passes the turn without opening a bet. Embido proposes a bet; Gehiago raises it. Your team can bluff with its bets, but must never send a false sign.",
  "menuRespondingTiraAndIduki": "Responding: Tira and Iduki",
  "menuWhenFacingABetIdukiAcceptsTheCardsWill": "When facing a bet, Iduki accepts: the cards will decide the winner at scoring. Tira refuses: the phase ends and the opponent scores the refusal points based on previous bets. A raise proposes a higher bet instead.",
  "menuHordagoTheWholeRound": "Hordago: the whole round",
  "menuHordagoPutsTheEntireRoundAtStakeIfAccepted": "Hordago puts the entire round at stake. If accepted with Iduki, hands are compared immediately for this phase and the winner takes the round. Tira refuses the challenge and concedes only refusal points. You will bet 2 at High and Pairs, then call a raise at Game. Other choices stay disabled until free play.",
  "menuYourTurnToCall": "Your turn to call",
  "menuYourOpponentRaisesBy8TheBetGoesFrom": "Your opponent raises by 8: the bet goes from 2 to 10 stones. Click Iduki to accept. The cards will decide the winner at scoring.",
  "roundScoring": "Scoring",
  "menuTheCardsAreRevealedBetsAndPointsForPairs": "The cards are revealed. Bets and points for Pairs and Game are added up. The first team to reach 40 stones wins the round.",
  "menuHighHandia": "High — Handia",
  "menuCompareCardsFromHighestToLowestTheKingIs": "Compare cards from highest to lowest. The King is strongest. Click Bet 2 to propose two stones. An opponent will accept this first bet.",
  "menuLowTtipia": "Low — Ttipia",
  "menuNowCompareTheLowestCardsTheAceIsBest": "Now compare the lowest cards. The Ace is best. If tied, compare the next cards; Esku breaks a perfect tie.",
  "menuPairsPareak": "Pairs — Pareak",
  "menuTwoMatchingCardsMakeAPairThreeMakeMediak": "Two matching cards make a pair; three make Mediak; two pairs or four matching cards make Dobliak. Only players with pairs take part. You have two Kings: Bai announces your pair. Click Bet 2 to defend it.",
  "menuGameJoko": "Game — Joko",
  "menuFaceCardsAreWorth10AndOtherCardsTheir": "Face cards are worth 10 and other cards their face value. You need at least 31. The best Game total is 31, then 32. If nobody has Game, play Point, aiming closest to 30. Bet 2 here: an opponent will raise and you will learn to call with Iduki.",
